<section id="word-headings">
  <section>
    <h1>Heading Structure</h1>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Use heading styles</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>Use headings to structure document</li>
      <li>Use predefined styles</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section>
    <img
      src="https://images.anysurfer.be/applications/Word365/heading_styles.jpg"
      alt="Use predefined heading styles in Word -ADOD technique 5"
    />
    <p>Home > Styles > Heading 1 (or Heading 2, 3, ...6)</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Why ?</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Automatic table of contents</li>
      <li>Structure available for screenreader</li>
      <li>Allow screenreader user to jump to a heading</li>
      <li>Easy to change appearance of a type of heading in whole document</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Pay attention</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>Don't skip heading levels</li>
      <li>Only mark real headings as headings</li>
      <li>You can modify the appearance of the heading styles</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Modify styles</h2>
  </section>

  <section>
    <img
      src="https://images.anysurfer.be/applications/Word365/modify_heading_style.jpg"
      alt=""
    />
    <p>Right click on a style > Modify</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <img
      src="https://images.anysurfer.be/applications/Word365/modify_heading_style2.jpg"
      alt=""
    />
    <p>Use the formatting options</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h3>Tip</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Define spacing before and after a heading in heading style</li>

      <li>Don't add spaces manually with ENTER</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <img
      src="https://images.anysurfer.be/applications/Word365/paragraph_spacing.jpg"
      alt="Paragraph dialog window"
    />
    <p>Modify style > Paragraph > spacing</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Update heading style to match selection</h2>
    <img
      src="https://images.anysurfer.be/applications/Word365/update_heading.jpg"
      alt="Update heading3 to look like selected text in document"
    />

    <p>Styles > right click on style > Update Heading X to match selection</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Control heading styles with outline view</h2>
    <ol class="word">
      <li>File > Options > Advanced</li>
      <li>Find the Display section</li>
      <li>
        Set ' Style area pane width in Draft and Outline Views' to 2,5 cm.
      </li>
      <li>Click OK</li>
      <li>View > Draft</li>
      <li>In the left column the heading levels are displayed.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>
  <section>
    <img
      src="https://images.anysurfer.be/applications/Word365/word_options_draft_pane.png"
      alt="Style area pane width in Draft and Outline Views set to 4 cm in Word options"
    />
  </section>

  <section>
    <img
      src="https://images.anysurfer.be/applications/Word365/outline_example_edf.jpg"
      alt="EDF word document with outline showing headings "
    />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Control heading styles with navigation pane</h2>
    <img
      src="https://images.anysurfer.be/applications/Word365/navigation_pane.jpg"
      alt="Navigation pane for EDF document showing table of contents"
    />
    <p>View > check "Navigation pane"</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Exercise : headings</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Start from the file created in the previous exercise</li>
      <li>Use heading styles to structure the document</li>
      <li>Customize the styles to your taste</li>
      <li>Use the draft view to check heading levels</li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</section>
